<title>POLAND: MOST POLISH MINIMUM T-BILL PRICES FALL AT TENDER.</title>
<headline>MOST POLISH MINIMUM T-BILL PRICES FALL AT TENDER.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of most Polish</p>
<p>T-bills fell at today's primary auction despite total demand of</p>
<p>1.82 billion zlotys, exceeding the treasury's 1.3 billion zloty</p>
<p>offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The Treasury sold a total of 1.12 billion zlotys worth of</p>
<p>the bills.</p>
<p>   T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week 52-week</p>
<p>   new min price   96.75    94.95    90.40     --	82.35</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)  (96.75)  (95.00)  (90.48)    --     (82.45)</p>
<p>   new max price   96.90    95.20    90.53     --	83.18</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)  (97.02)  (95.30)  (90.80)    --     (83.18)</p>
<p>   offer	     400.0    200.0    200.0     --	500.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded   884.5    162.7     46.3     --	723.0</p>
<p>   bids accepted   727.2     91.2     25.7     --	274.4</p>
<p>   next auction     --	400.0    200.0     --	600.0</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
